==Trivia==
*Zenyatta is one of [[Chris Metzen]]'s favorite heroes in the game.<ref name = "Transcript3">2014-11-24, [http://overwatch.blizzplanet.com/blog/comments/blizzcon-2014-overwatch-unveiled-panel-transcript/3 BlizzCon 2014 – Overwatch Unveiled Panel Transcript]. ''Blizzplanet'', accessed on 2015-03-08</ref>
*Zenyatta is one of three heroes with no footstep sounds, as he floats instead of walking. The others are [[Sigma]] and [[Echo]].

===Cultural References===
*The healing aspect of his orbs and the chime-like sound they make may take inspiration from [[Wikipedia:Baoding balls|Baoding balls]], also known as Chinese medicine balls, among other names. They are popular among advocates as a form of alternative medicine for stress relief and improving dexterity and strength in the hands.
*Zenyatta's name has been observed to be a combination of the word "Zen", which is the Japanese name for Chan Buddhism, and "Śūnyatā", which means "emptiness" in Pali, a Buddhist concept referring to the idea that the world is without a true essence or sense of self.
**It's also likely a reference to the The Police album ''Zenyatta Mondatta'', considering his late counterpart's name is Mondatta.
**The name they share between Mondatta and Zenyatta, "Tekhartha," could play off of the name of the Buddha before he achieved nirvana, Siddhartha Gautama, and "Tek" pronounced like "Tech" as a play on the fact that they are robots.
*A number of players have likened the relationship between Zenyatta and [[Ramattra]] as akin to [https://marvel.fandom.com/wiki/Professor_X Charles Xavier] and [https://marvel.fandom.com/wiki/Magneto Magneto] from ''X-Men''.<ref>2022-11-08, [https://www.kotaku.com.au/2022/11/overwatch-2-reveals-new-hero-ramattra-locked-behind-battle-pass/ Overwatch 2 Reveals New Hero Ramattra, Locked Behind Battle Pass]. ''Kotaku'', accessed on 2022-11-10</ref>
*Zenyatta's Cultist and Zealot skins are both references to the fictional cosmic entity [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cthulhu Cthulhu]. This is especially apparent with Zenyatta having tentacles for a mouth, which is identical to the visual depiction of Cthulhu.

===Misc. Character Information===
*Zenyatta believes that as long as free will exists, there will always be evil in the world, yet to deny free will would also be evil. He has the ability to dream.<ref name = "OW2ZenyattaQuotes">''[[Overwatch 2]]'', ''[[Zenyatta/Quotes|Zenyatta Quotes]]''</ref>
*Zenyatta found humans' manner of speech perplexing at first, having little grasp of metaphors. He still occasionally struggles with their figures of speech.<ref name = "StoneByStone">''[[Stone By Stone]]''</ref>
*Like all Shambali, despite being unable to eat, Zenyatta knows how to prepare food.<ref name = "Cookbook">''[[Overwatch: The Official Cookbook]]''</ref> 
*Zenyatta likes being near the coast, as it reminds him of where he was constructed.<ref name = "OW2ZenyattaQuotes"/>

====Disputed Information====
*In a gameplay trailer for ''[[Overwatch 2]]'', Zenyatta was seen working for Talon against his will, and reuniting with Genji, leading to a battle against Talon forces. The events were apparently due to occur in [[Story Missions]].<ref name = "OW2Gameplay">2019-11-01, [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dZl1yGUetjI Overwatch 2 Gameplay Trailer]. ''YouTube'', accessed on 2019-11-08</ref> With Story Missions apparently cancelled (or at least de-prioritized under Microsoft),<ref name = "StoryCancelled">2024-03-18, [https://kotaku.com/overwatch-2-story-missions-campaign-canceled-blizzard-1851345720 Overwatch 2 Devs Fear Story Missions Have Been Canceled]. ''Kotaku'', accessed on 2024-04-01</ref> the canonicity of these events is dubious.
*In [[Venture]]'s gameplay trailer, Zenyatta is again seen working with Talon at [[Petra]] against Overwatch, before Overwatch forces Talon to retreat with Venture's help.<ref name = "VentureNew">2024-03-28, [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JF6tLqe_FSA Venture | New Hero Gameplay Trailer | Overwatch 2]. ''YouTube'', accessed on 2024-03-28</ref>

